PLAN_JOURNAL.unshift({"id":"resume-evidence-boundary-whatsapp-2026-11-10","area":"resume","updated":"2026-11-10T07:28:09Z","title":"Stop unverified JD experience claims from reaching WhatsApp delivery","approval":"proposed","delivery":"in progress","detail":"A source audit found that tailor.ts still told the model to write every JD term into experience and to treat the candidate as claiming the entire JD, while the mandatory role-weaving pass used all scoreKws instead of evidence-supported jdKwsPrompt. The Gemini-related pass could add terms without confirming they appeared in the source resume or explicit first-person confirmations. Separately, unverified_jd_terms was allowed as a WhatsApp shortfall, so a draft with unsupported experience claims could still be considered sendable. PR #279 corrects the prompt, per-role weaving and related-term filter, and makes unverified experience claims use the existing same-account resume fallback. The separate labelled Job-post terms line and the 70% WhatsApp gap policy / 95% supported-coverage clean-pass rule are preserved.","evidence":"PR #279 draft at head cc7e4ea675d808a89f4b4ea1f22711b0be7141b7. It adds regressions for unverified claims not being sendable and for evidence-bound prompt/related-term behavior. Kompas baseline 42775486253, full CI 42775486431 and WhatsApp recovery regression 42775486380 are all IN PROGRESS; Vercel status is pending. No live model call, resume write, R2 write, email, WhatsApp send or production deployment.","next":"Wait for exact-head CI and preview status. The change affects WhatsApp external sending, so keep PR #279 draft and obtain explicit owner review before merge/deployment. Verify same-account fallback after approval without sending a real message.","commit":"cc7e4ea675d808a89f4b4ea1f22711b0be7141b7"})

