PLAN_JOURNAL.unshift({"id":"actions-artifact-storage-2026-11-13","area":"kompas","updated":"2026-11-13T00:55:00.000Z","title":"Delete the Kompas Windows Actions artifact backlog","approval":"approved","delivery":"in progress","detail":"Owner Eshwar explicitly approved deleting all old Actions artifacts except the newest Kompas-Windows-Caption-Once build. The caption workflow had uploaded about 162 MB on pull requests and kept each copy for 14 days. Retention is now 1 day, and the upload runs only on a push to master or a manual run. A master push that does not change legacy/perfact/desktop or public/kompas does not build, so the kompas-desktop-latest release asset is left as it was. ci.yml already used retention-days 1 and nextjs-ci.yml already used retention-days 3. The cleanup workflow is manual-only. No website screen changed. No production deploy was requested, and no commit message uses a ship marker.","evidence":"Before cleanup: 151 non-expired artifacts, 24,462,128,863 bytes, zero expired. Cleanup run 43339668406 deleted 150 artifacts (24,300,087,723 bytes, 24.300 GB) and 3 Actions caches (417,444,083 bytes). After cleanup the only artifact is Kompas-Windows-Caption-Once-36053e2a02bb8b648bec40ebd71449d86902f127, id 13996119819, 162,041,140 bytes, created 2026-11-13T00:22:25Z. Caches remaining: 0. Release tag kompas-desktop-latest still has Kompas.exe updated_at 2026-11-12T22:50:32Z, size 162,248,232. Pull request 340's Windows build skipped the upload step and the release step. parfAct is private and the Actions token returned HTTP 404, so its artifacts were not deleted. Its workflows still set retention-days 14 on kompas-desktop-windows-x64 and kompas-desktop-candidate.","next":"parfAct still needs an Actions token that can see the private repo before its old artifacts can be deleted and its retention lowered to 1-3 days. Do not replace kompas-desktop-latest while doing that."})

