PLAN_JOURNAL.unshift({"id":"gmail-notify-export-owner-scope-worker-off-switch-2026-11-13","area":"gmail","updated":"2026-11-13T12:25:00Z","title":"Secure Gmail notification export and enforce the disabled background-worker gate","approval":"approved","delivery":"in progress","detail":"The Poke-inspired Gmail work is multi-account and account/thread scoped. PR #359 merged into canonical master as 14bc372f579b87197df77d48c8645759a12d7caa. The formerly public notify-rules export is now gated by GMAIL_UPDATES_SCHEDULER_ENABLED and a constant-time CRON_SECRET bearer check, returns private/no-store data grouped by owner and receiving inbox, and does not merge senders across accounts. The unattended tick returns 503 before storage scans or delivery unless both the scheduler flag and approved WHATSAPP_GMAIL_UPDATE_TEMPLATE are present; CRON_SECRET remains mandatory. No environment values were changed, no scheduler was created, and no notification worker was enabled.","evidence":"PR #359 exact head ab3e070aeb4ca8864f5f34ae26fd4c761a645792 passed full CI 43419089019, Plan Journal/REA schema 43419089029 and Kompas baseline 43419089067. Merge commit 14bc372f579b87197df77d48c8645759a12d7caa is on master. A first Vercel deployment dpl_AHuMVDuxLUvJZVFtZsaVsgbo3Qji cloned the merge SHA but was canceled before build because the Ignored Build Step requires [ship] in the commit message. A release-marker commit 5fe6e8181f7a4366ae61a07a70f0d822fcb0e07c then began a production build, but it was canceled before completion to respect the active MFit Safe Merge Gate rule requiring an explicit owner decision for security-gate changes. The canonical alias remains READY on prior SHA 4c01951af59f7d64eecd2b39da32d75c607d9eea; therefore the security fix is merged but not deployed. Read-only runtime evidence remains 48 HTTP 402 responses from the formerly public export path in the preceding 24 hours; no caller was identified or contacted.","next":"Obtain explicit owner approval for the production rollout of PR #359's security boundary, then create one [ship] release commit and verify a READY production deployment, canonical alias SHA, and fail-closed 503 behavior for export and tick while the scheduler remains disabled. Do not configure the scheduler/template, identify or contact the unknown caller, or send any email/WhatsApp notification. Real two-inbox and mobile acceptance remains separate.","commit":"14bc372f579b87197df77d48c8645759a12d7caa"});

